WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:02.010
- [Instructor] So we're
given this equation here.

00:02.010 --> 00:03.940
And what I want you to
do is pause this video

00:03.940 --> 00:05.050
and see if you can solve it.

00:05.050 --> 00:07.573
What x values satisfy the equation?

00:08.660 --> 00:11.010
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:11.010 --> 00:12.620
So one technique could be

00:12.620 --> 00:13.970
just, let's just try to complete

00:13.970 --> 00:16.440
the square here on the left-hand side.

00:16.440 --> 00:18.320
So to do that, let me write it this way,

00:18.320 --> 00:21.910
x squared minus eight x.

00:21.910 --> 00:24.410
And then I have,

00:24.410 --> 00:27.660
I'll write the plus one out here, is equal

00:27.660 --> 00:30.630
to 85.

00:30.630 --> 00:32.150
Now if I wanna complete the square,

00:32.150 --> 00:33.007
I just have to think,

00:33.007 --> 00:35.517
"What can I add to both
sides of this equation

00:35.517 --> 00:37.777
"that could make this part
of the left-hand expression

00:37.777 --> 00:39.310
"a perfect square?"

00:39.310 --> 00:41.170
Well, if I look at this
negative eight coefficient

00:41.170 --> 00:42.707
on the first-degree term, I could say,

00:42.707 --> 00:44.220
"Okay, let me take half
of negative eight."

00:44.220 --> 00:45.990
That would be negative four.

00:45.990 --> 00:49.400
And then, negative four squared
is going to be positive 16.

00:49.400 --> 00:52.250
So I'm gonna add positive
16 on the left-hand side.

00:52.250 --> 00:55.180
And if I want, I could then subtract a 16

00:55.180 --> 00:56.520
from the left-hand side.

00:56.520 --> 00:59.280
Or I could add a 16 on
the right-hand side.

00:59.280 --> 01:00.700
Notice, I've just done the same thing

01:00.700 --> 01:02.860
to both sides of this equation.

01:02.860 --> 01:04.760
And why was that useful?

01:04.760 --> 01:06.030
Well, now what I've just put

01:06.030 --> 01:08.620
in parentheses is a perfect square.

01:08.620 --> 01:12.240
This is the same thing
as x minus four squared.

01:12.240 --> 01:13.280
It was by design.

01:13.280 --> 01:14.280
We looked at that negative eight.

01:14.280 --> 01:16.420
Half of that is negative four.

01:16.420 --> 01:17.790
You square it, you get 16.

01:17.790 --> 01:20.580
And you can verify, x minus
four times x minus four is,

01:20.580 --> 01:22.400
indeed, equal to this.

01:22.400 --> 01:25.020
And then we have plus one is going

01:25.020 --> 01:28.430
to be equal to, what's 85 plus 16?

01:28.430 --> 01:31.010
That is 101.

01:31.010 --> 01:32.680
And now we wanna get rid of this one

01:32.680 --> 01:33.520
on the left-hand side.

01:33.520 --> 01:35.180
And the easiest way we
can do that is subtract

01:35.180 --> 01:36.290
one from both sides.

01:36.290 --> 01:40.080
That way we'll just isolate
that x minus four squared.

01:40.080 --> 01:43.563
And we are left with x minus four squared.

01:44.900 --> 01:48.160
Four squared, these cancel out, is going

01:48.160 --> 01:50.143
to be equal to 100.

01:51.890 --> 01:55.030
Now if something squared is equal to 100,

01:55.030 --> 01:57.140
that means that the something is equal

01:57.140 --> 01:59.940
to the positive or the negative
square root of a hundred.

01:59.940 --> 02:04.060
Or that that something,
x minus four, is equal

02:04.060 --> 02:07.870
to positive or negative 10.

02:07.870 --> 02:09.560
Positive or negative 10.

02:09.560 --> 02:10.610
All I did is took the plus

02:10.610 --> 02:12.130
or minus square root of a hundred.

02:12.130 --> 02:13.180
And this makes sense.

02:13.180 --> 02:16.110
If I took positive 10
squared, I'll get a hundred.

02:16.110 --> 02:17.790
If I take negative 10
squared, I get a hundred.

02:17.790 --> 02:20.810
So x minus four could
be either one of those.

02:20.810 --> 02:25.120
And now I just add four to
both sides of the equation.

02:25.120 --> 02:27.050
And then what do I get?

02:27.050 --> 02:30.570
I get x is equal

02:30.570 --> 02:35.570
to four plus or minus 10.

02:35.770 --> 02:37.130
Or another way of thinking about it,

02:37.130 --> 02:39.250
I could write it as x is equal

02:39.250 --> 02:41.950
to, four plus 10 is 14.

02:41.950 --> 02:46.230
And then four minus 10
is equal to negative six.

02:46.230 --> 02:48.440
So these are two ways to solve it.

02:48.440 --> 02:51.360
But there's other ways
to solve this equation.

02:51.360 --> 02:53.670
We could, right from the get-go, try

02:53.670 --> 02:57.000
to subtract 85 from both sides.

02:57.000 --> 02:59.250
Some people feel more
comfortable solving quadratics

02:59.250 --> 03:03.390
if they have that quadratic
expression be equal to zero.

03:03.390 --> 03:06.890
And if you did that, you
would get x squared minus

03:06.890 --> 03:10.940
eight x minus 84 is equal to zero.

03:10.940 --> 03:14.060
All I did is I subtracted
85 from both sides

03:14.060 --> 03:16.590
of this equation to get
this right over here.

03:16.590 --> 03:18.790
Now this one we can approach
in two different ways.

03:18.790 --> 03:21.050
We can complete the square again.

03:21.050 --> 03:23.280
Or we could just try to factor.

03:23.280 --> 03:24.310
If we complete the square,

03:24.310 --> 03:26.010
we're going to see something
very similar to this.

03:26.010 --> 03:28.080
Actually, let me just do that really fast.

03:28.080 --> 03:30.540
If I look at this part, right over there,

03:30.540 --> 03:35.250
I could say x squared minus eight x.

03:35.250 --> 03:36.320
And then once again,

03:36.320 --> 03:37.990
half of negative eight is negative four.

03:37.990 --> 03:40.240
That squared is plus 16.

03:40.240 --> 03:42.480
And then I'd have minus 84.

03:42.480 --> 03:43.950
So let me do that in that blue color

03:43.950 --> 03:45.830
so we can keep track.

03:45.830 --> 03:47.690
Minus 84.

03:47.690 --> 03:50.500
And then if I added 16
on the left-hand side,

03:50.500 --> 03:52.330
I could either add that
to the right-hand side

03:52.330 --> 03:54.840
so both sides have 16 added to it.

03:54.840 --> 03:57.230
Or if I wanna maintain the equality,

03:57.230 --> 04:00.780
I could just subtract 16
from the left-hand side.

04:00.780 --> 04:02.410
So I've added 16, subtracted 16.

04:02.410 --> 04:05.010
I haven't changed the
left-hand side's value.

04:05.010 --> 04:07.490
And then that would be equal to zero.

04:07.490 --> 04:09.280
This part right over here,

04:09.280 --> 04:12.600
this is x minus four squared.

04:12.600 --> 04:15.080
This part right over here is

04:15.080 --> 04:19.700
minus 100 is equal to zero.

04:19.700 --> 04:21.810
And then you add a hundred
to both sides of this

04:21.810 --> 04:24.940
and you get exactly this
step right over here.

04:24.940 --> 04:26.910
Now another way that we
could've approached it

04:26.910 --> 04:28.740
without completing the square.

04:28.740 --> 04:31.460
We could've said x squared minus

04:31.460 --> 04:34.730
eight x minus 84 is equal to zero.

04:34.730 --> 04:36.670
And think about what two numbers

04:36.670 --> 04:39.240
if I multiply them I get negative 84.

04:39.240 --> 04:40.680
So they'd have to have different signs,

04:40.680 --> 04:42.780
since when I take their product
I get a negative number.

04:42.780 --> 04:45.930
And when I add them together
I get negative eight.

04:45.930 --> 04:47.680
And there we could just
look at the factorization

04:47.680 --> 04:50.730
of negative 84, of 84 generally.

04:50.730 --> 04:53.390
It could be two times,
let's just think about 84.

04:53.390 --> 04:56.090
84 could be two times 42.

04:56.090 --> 04:58.010
And obviously, one of them
would have to be negative,

04:58.010 --> 04:59.350
one of them would have to be positive

04:59.350 --> 05:01.260
in order to get to negative 84.

05:01.260 --> 05:03.300
But the difference
between these two numbers,

05:03.300 --> 05:05.410
if one was positive
and one was negative is

05:05.410 --> 05:06.820
a lot more than eight.

05:06.820 --> 05:08.260
So that doesn't work.

05:08.260 --> 05:11.580
So let's try, let's see,
I'll do a few in my head.

05:11.580 --> 05:14.220
Three times 28.

05:14.220 --> 05:16.850
But still that difference
is way more than eight.

05:16.850 --> 05:21.850
Four times, four times,
let's see, (mumbles).

05:21.920 --> 05:23.860
Four times 21, no, that difference

05:23.860 --> 05:26.490
between four and 21 is
still larger than eight.

05:26.490 --> 05:28.180
Let's see, five doesn't go into it.

05:28.180 --> 05:32.140
Six times 14, that's interesting now.

05:32.140 --> 05:33.910
Okay, so let's think about this.

05:33.910 --> 05:37.540
So six times 14 is equal to 84.

05:37.540 --> 05:39.000
One of them has to be negative.

05:39.000 --> 05:42.630
And since when we take the
sum of the two numbers,

05:42.630 --> 05:43.480
we get a negative number,

05:43.480 --> 05:45.620
that means the larger one is negative.

05:45.620 --> 05:48.830
So let's see, six times
negative 14 is negative 84.

05:48.830 --> 05:51.590
Six plus negative 14 is,

05:51.590 --> 05:54.330
indeed, equal to negative eight.

05:54.330 --> 05:59.180
So we can factor this as x plus six times

05:59.180 --> 06:03.360
x minus 14 is equal to zero.

06:03.360 --> 06:05.790
And so the product of those
two things is equal to zero.

06:05.790 --> 06:08.980
That means if either of
them is equal to zero,

06:08.980 --> 06:11.840
that would make the entire
expression equal to zero.

06:11.840 --> 06:14.910
So we could say x plus
six is equal to zero.

06:14.910 --> 06:18.140
Or x minus 14 is equal to zero.

06:18.140 --> 06:19.710
Subtract six from both sides here.

06:19.710 --> 06:21.510
We get x is equal to negative six.

06:21.510 --> 06:23.690
Or add 14 to both sides here.

06:23.690 --> 06:25.870
Or x is equal to 14.

06:25.870 --> 06:27.573
Exactly what we got up here.
